## Lore

The Drizzit look like Earth grasshoppers scaled up to giant size, tall and
lanky with powerful jumping legs, and they are far more intelligent than
their appearance suggests. Their coloring runs from pale green to sandy
brown and darkens in winter. Females carry a large hood that protects their
wings. Folk on Rifts Earth call them Hopper Bugs, because hopping is how
they get anywhere in a hurry, though they can walk and run upright as well.

They cannot form human words; their mouths manage only pops, clicks and
whistles. Instead they rub their hairy forearms together to make a pleasant
chirping, and by changing its pitch and volume they can send messages a
long way.

At home the Drizzit are farmers above all, a people without nations, greed
or envy, who have never known war or famine. That peaceful upbringing has
left them badly prepared for Rifts Earth. They would rather flee and
resettle than fight, but they are not pacifists and will fight to the death
when cornered. A few have taken up magic to protect themselves and their
crops.

## GM Notes

Size: males 6-8 feet (1.8 to 2.4 m), females 8-12 feet (2.4 to 3.6 m).
Weight: males 160 to 180 pounds (72 to 81 kg), females 200 to 320 pounds
(90 to 144 kg). Life span 2D4+32 years for males, 3D4+38 for females; adult
at 10. Females bear 2D4+16 young at a time, as often as every 6 months.

Horror Factor 10, or 13 when mistaken for Xiticix.

Disposition: peaceful, friendly and tolerant; a culture built on growing
fruit, which they eat almost exclusively. No hunting or predatory instincts.

Habitat: temperate climates and rainforests, wherever fruit grows; mainly
between the Magic Zone, Dinosaur Swamp and the Deep South, with a large
community in South America. Slave market value: low, 1D4x1,000 credits.

Allies: none as such, but they give every race the benefit of the doubt and
get on best with farmers and wilderness folk. Enemies: they despise the
Xiticix, dislike heavy industry and avoid the Coalition States.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'drizzit');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'drizzit';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-drizzit-class.sql');
